==Enemy==
Zamelle moves slower than Camelle and attacks less frequently, but is only knocked back when killed. While she does not burrow, she can revive an infinite amount of times if she isn't finished for good, and her Base Destroyer ability can make her quite dangerous if you're losing ground.

==Strategy==
Although Zamelle may seem intimidating, she is not very threatening on her own due to her slow attack rate, and can be quite literally killed off by a group of [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Sifu Cats]]. The problem arises when she is supporting other threats, as it would be difficult to get an opening and finish her off for good since her singular knockback doesn't allow for the best timing. More often than not, you'll have to deal with her the hard way, that being killing everything else, as her high range means not many units will be safe.

Despite lacking the [[Zombie Killer]] ability, [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] is a great unit to use against Zamelle, as it can possibly reach and attack her several times for its low cost. Its [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed variant]] works much better, thanks to being Strong Against Zombies and having Zombie Killer. [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan Cat]] and [[Brainwashed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Mythic Titan]] can also be used in a similar capacity.

If you are unable to permanently kill Zamelle, use fast units like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Giraffe Cat]], or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to bypass her before she could rise up again. Just beware that cheesing strategies are not always effective in some cases. Alternatively, these units can be used to deal damage before you get the last hit in with a [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer unit]] or [[Holy Blast]]. Chipping her down with [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Omni Strike Cats|Omni Strike]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] units may also be feasible, provided that she is heavily supported.

[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] that deal well with this enemy are [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rushers]] and [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tankers]], such as [[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]] (especially in [[True Form]]) and [[Seashore Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Seashore Kai]], and snipers that can somehow reach her like [[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Sharpshooter Saki]].

